# Wholesale Acquisition Engine — provider credentials
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values from YOUR OWN provider
# accounts. .env is git-ignored; never commit real keys, and never paste a
# key into source code.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# The engine runs fully without any of these. With nothing set it says
# "No live property-data provider configured. Running in CSV/test mode."
# and works from your CSV files exactly as it does today.
#
# No vendor is chosen for you. Picking one means reading that vendor's
# official API documentation, terms of service and pricing first — the
# endpoint and auth scheme below come from those docs, not from a guess.
# Use documented APIs with your own account, honour the published rate
# limits, and do not scrape sites or work around CAPTCHAs, robots.txt,
# logins, paywalls or anti-bot measures.

# --- property search + detail ---------------------------------------------
# Both are required before a live search will run.
# PROPERTY_DATA_BASE_URL is the API root from your vendor's documentation,
# e.g. https://api.your-provider.example/v1 — there is no default.
PROPERTY_DATA_API_KEY=
PROPERTY_DATA_BASE_URL=

# --- public records (liens, tax status, foreclosure filings) --------------
# Optional. Without it, distress signals stay as reported by the lead source
# and are labelled unverified. Nothing is ever invented to fill the gap.
PUBLIC_RECORDS_API_KEY=

# --- comparable sales ------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Without it, supply comps by CSV or the ARV stays SOURCE-PROVIDED
# and the deal cannot clear the verification gate.
COMPS_API_KEY=

# --- skip tracing ----------------------------------------------------------
# NOT CONNECTED. The interface exists; no provider is wired to it. Setting
# this does not enable contact lookups, and the engine will never generate a
# phone number or email address.
SKIP_TRACE_API_KEY=
